        "text": "CHAPTER 9 Connecting to the Internet 171\nThe output, shown in Figure 9-5, provides information about what ping is doing.\nIf the ping can\u2019t reach the host, you receive a message that the host is unreach-\nable. If the ping can reach the host, you receive feedback that provides how long it\ntakes \u2014 in milliseconds (ms) \u2014 for the signal from your computer to get to the\ndestination computer and back again. (The lower the numbers, the better.) For\ncomputers connected to the same local network, a ping time of 1 ms to 3 ms is an\nacceptable response time. For dialup connections, expect somewhere around\n150 ms. When you start seeing ping times climbing to 900 ms or higher, the net-\nwork is likely under heavy use (or you have something wrong with your cables).",
